 flare-up at the country's  parliament today crews were back at it  trying to get the upper hand on a  devastating fire that was believed to be  under control officials had warned of  flare-ups because of all the carpets and  wood floors in the building on sunday  the roof of the old wing which dates  back to 1884 partially collapsed the  building is also home to thousands of  historic books photos and works of art a  49 year old man has been charged with  arson and theft  still ahead could an old deal help  shield prince andrew from a civil  [Music]  lawsuit a newly unsealed deal could  possibly impact a lawsuit against prince  andrew the 2009 legal settlement between  convicted sex offender jeffrey epstein  and the woman accusing prince andrew of  forcing her into sex as a teenager has  been made public in it epstein agrees to  pay virginia due for a half a million  dollars if she agrees not to sue him or  anyone as redmond shannon reports a  judge will hear arguments tomorrow on  whether due phrase civil case can  proceed  despite this now infamous picture prince  andrew has always maintained his  innocence  i have no recollection of ever meeting  this lady his accuser virginia dufrey  says the duke of york forced her into  sex three times when she was under 18.  she says she was trafficked by the  prince's friends convicted sex offenders  jeffrey epstein and epstein's girlfriend  gelaine maxwell in 2019 epstein died in  prison last week maxwell was convicted  of sex trafficking young girls we're  told constantly you know these people  will never go to jail they're too  powerful they're too rich this is not  the end this is just the beginning  andrew has not been accused of any  criminal wrongdoing his lawyers will  argue before a judge tuesday that  epstein's 2009 settlement with dufres  shields the prince from her civil  lawsuit in the newly published document  epstein agreed to pay you for 500 000  u.s dollars if she agreed not to sue any  other person or entity who could have  been included as a potential defendant  from all manner of legal action that is  just so vague and bizarre to me lawyer  lisa bloom represented eight of  epstein's victims she says the judge  should allow duprey's case against  andrew to proceed despite the epstein  deal i think it would be wrong and a  violation of essential principles of  contract law to have prince andrew  released because he's not mentioned by  name anywhere in the agreement even if  andrew's lawyers succeed royal watchers  think the damage is done i think  regardless of what happens in the next  couple of days in the states prince  andrew's career as a working royal is  sadly over  i think he's finished his reputation is  in such tatters that i really don't  think he can come back from this if the  case does go ahead it's not expected to  begin until september redmond shannon  global news london  hong kong's free press suffered another  blow today with the online site citizen  news announcing it is shutting down the  publication says the decision was made  over the safety of its reporters after  police raided pro-democracy outlet stan  news last month arresting staff members  on sedition charges this is the third  outlet to shutter in recent months in  hong kong press freedoms in hong kong  have been deteriorating since beijing  introduced a sweeping national security  law in 2020  starting tomorrow many blackberry mobile  phones will stop reliably working the  company has decommissioned several of  its services devices using old software  through wi-fi connections could now have  trouble making phone calls sending text  messages and accessing 9-1-1 the change  will not impact phones running on  android software blackberry first  announced it would end some services in  2020 as part of its transition towards a  software company  turning junk into gems next the bc man  giving plastic an artsy new purpose  a new brunswick wildlife shelter is  starting off 2022 with a rare rescue it  took in a black vulture for the first  time in a facebook post the atlantic  wildlife institute says the bird was  found new year's day in moncton unable  to fly it has a severe eye injury black  vultures are more common in warmer  climates like south america but  sightings in the maritimes have risen in  recent years  the city of vancouver is doing its part  to help keep plastic bags out of  landfills on january 1st vancouver  became the latest canadian city to ban  single-use plastic bags it's a dramatic  shift for some but for one bc man it's  just second nature he's been doing his  part to keep them out of the trash for  decades and all he needs is an artistic  touch jay durant explains  for the past year roger brenneckmeyer  has been turning people's trash into  someone else's treasure taking plastic  bags and overwrap and creating beautiful  pieces of art  so this amount of plastic turns into  that this environmentally conscious  career is decades in the making in the  late 80s roger helped his high school  launch its first recycling program he  ended up working in corporate  communications printing reports and  brochures that got him thinking about  damage to the forests and then something  clicked i kind of had a jerry maguire  moment this moment will be the moment of  something real  and fun  and i said you know what i'm actually  part of a problem here not part of the  solution  to date roger figures he saved about 150  000 plastic bags from the landfill this  installation at a senior's home in  richmond used about 18 thousand bags  they get to go down to breakfast every  morning and look up and see a beautiful  wisteria tree knowing that their trash  is actually part of that  that beautiful mosaic  now he's working on a new technique to  turn bigger ocean plastics like fishing  nets and crab baskets into art hoping to  inspire others to look at this type of  business idea  maybe they don't do art but maybe they  create uh  plates or stools or or whatnot just as  long as we are taking something that is  deemed landfill and transforming it into  something that is beautiful that is  useful  anyone ordering a piece can hand over  their own plastic bags if not roger  still has so much to get through  we can actually create new product  out of something that is going straight  to the to the garbage can  you know building a little treasure out  of a lot of trash  jay durant global news  beautiful in more ways than one and that  is global national for this monday night  i'm nitu garcia tonight's your canada is  the village of caroline alberta there  are beautiful spots all over canada  please email yours to viewers at  globalnational.com  thanks for watching have a great night
 

